f=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1333318-what-kind-of-powers-do-you-think-scions-in-mythos-will-have?p=1333470#post1333470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know nothing about the Mythos so does 'ghoul' have any particular connotations to it or is it just 'Angry Zombie That Eats People'?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're a race of (usually subterranean) humanoids with a somewhat canine like appearance who eat corpses. IIRC, it's also implied that they sometimes do the &quot;changeling&quot; trick of swapping out one of their own offspring for a human baby. They first appear in the short story &quot;Pickman's Model&quot;, which is one I tend to recommend to people not familiar with Lovecraft's work as it is, 1) a pretty good story, and 2) is really short. (I think the original Delta Green sourcebooks for the Call of Cthulhu RPG presented them as dwelling in NYC's subways and other underground tunnel systems.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T11:52:55-07:00","id":1333575,"title":"","content":"Does Body Horror count as a power?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1333318-what-kind-of-powers-do-you-think-scions-in-mythos-will-have?p=1333482#post1333482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're a race of (usually subterranean) humanoids with a somewhat canine like appearance who eat corpses. IIRC, it's also implied that they sometimes do the &quot;changeling&quot; trick of swapping out one of their own offspring for a human baby. They first appear in the short story &quot;Pickman's Model&quot;, which is one I tend to recommend to people not familiar with Lovecraft's work as it is, 1) a pretty good story, and 2) is really short. (I think the original Delta Green sourcebooks for the Call of Cthulhu RPG presented them as dwelling in NYC's subways and other underground tunnel systems.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Midnight_Meat_Train\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> tale from Clive Barker should fit in wonderfully, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-01-2019, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T12:08:56-07:00","id":1333577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"><